From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 17:44:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2723/2723] firmware: qcom: scm: Allow QSEECOM on the Anduril
 BlueChip

The Anduril BlueChip keeps its EFI variables behind the UEFI secure
application, as the Glymur CRD it is built on does. Add it to the
QSEECOM allowlist so that efivarfs and the PMIC RTC's UEFI time offset
work.

Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index 745b082..7df4536 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2303,6 +2303,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_scm_qseecom_allowlist[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "acer,swift-go-sfa14-11" },
 	{ .compatible = "acer,aspire-a14-11m" },
 	{ .compatible = "acer,aspire-a16-11m" },
+	{ .compatible = "anduril,bluechip" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,vivobook-s15" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,vivobook-s15-x1p4" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,vivobook-s16-s3607qa" },
-- 
2.56.0

